    <briefdescription>
<para>Specifies what happens with the contents of targets at the start and end of a render pass. On non-mobile platforms, the only choice that must be made is whether to clear or load the contents at the start of the pass. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A target without an entry loads and stores its contents. A resolve source loads its contents and discards them at the end. A resolve destination, a vrs attachment and a target that no subpass writes take no entry, because their actions are fixed. An entry for one of them is fatal.</para>
<para>On mobile devices, careful use of DontCare can avoid unnecessary memory traffic and improve both performance and thermals. Use with caution, as undefined contents are truly undefined and can lead to visual artifacts. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
